course: dictionary
lesson: 2535
title: Deer: one word, same plural
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words do not change when there is more than one. «Some words don't change at all: one sheep, two sheep; one deer, two deer.» You know how many there are from the number, not from an ending like -s.
explain: A deer is a wild animal with long thin legs and brown fur that eats plants and runs fast. Male deer, called stags or bucks, often have antlers, which fall off and grow back each year.
explain: Context helps you here too. «Rangers and scientists study droppings... deer droppings look like dark beans» tells you that deer are animals that leave droppings you can recognise, and that they are not the same as rabbit or fox droppings.
explain: Look for clues in phrases such as a herd of deer (a group), baby deer (a fawn) and deer park (a place where deer live). The words around deer tell you what is going on.
fact: Deer is a noun, and its plural is also deer.
fact: A group of deer is called a herd, and a baby deer is called a fawn.
fact: Deer are mammals that eat plants, which is why they are called herbivores.
fact: In safety, deer can jump into roads, especially at dawn and dusk, so take care when driving or walking near woods and fields.
fact: «Many prey, such as rabbits and deer, have eyes on the sides to see all around.» This helps them spot danger.
exercise: Which is correct? «One deer, two ___.» | *deer | deeres | deer's | deers
exercise: «Deer droppings look like dark beans.» What do deer droppings look like? | Fur and seeds | *Dark beans | Thin white strips | Little round balls
exercise: «Many prey, such as rabbits and deer, have eyes on the sides to see all around.» Why do deer have eyes on the sides? | To see only what is in front | *To see all around them | To read small print | To judge distance for hunting
test: What is a fawn? | A group of deer | A male deer with antlers | *A baby deer | A wild cat that hunts at night
test: How often do a stag's antlers grow back? | *Each year | Once in a lifetime | Every month | Never
exam: In the phrase «a herd of deer», which word tells you the group? | *herd | a | of | deer
